    "text": "Two balls&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are projected from the same position with horizontal velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> as shown. The separation between these two bodies at the moment their velocities become perpendicular to each other is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0019_bfd052047cd0.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" />"
  },
